## PROJECT CONTEXT

This sprint covers **UI Refactoring — Sprint 01: Live/Draft Separation & Unified Drafts view**.

Currently, drafts live in a separate shadow table for each seed (e.g. `content_articoli_drafts`). However, the dashboard does not provide a single, unified view to see all drafts across all seeds. Users have to navigate into each seed's page individually and look for entries with drafts.

This sprint will introduce:
1. A new backend endpoint `GET /api/content/drafts` that collects all drafts across all active seeds.
2. A static link in the main dashboard sidebar navbar to access a new "Drafts" section.
3. A unified page `/drafts` in the dashboard with a single `DataTable` view displaying all drafts showing: seed type (fruit type), seed entry name (fruit name), last modification date, and user who performed the last modification.
4. Actions on each row to quickly Edit, Publish, or Discard the draft.

==========================================================================
SECTION 1 — WHY THIS SPRINT EXISTS
==========================================================================

1. **UX Differentiation**: Users cannot easily see what work is currently in progress (draft) versus published. A centralized drafts drawer/page improves visibility and control over pending modifications.
2. **Simplified Audit & Review**: Content editors need a unified queue of drafts to review and approve before publishing them live, without hunting through every content category.

==========================================================================
SECTION 2 — CURRENT STATE & CODE REUSE
==========================================================================

1. **Schema Check**: In BeechCMS, a seed defines its structure. If `allowDrafts` is true, the D1 database creates a shadow table named `content_${slug}_drafts` to store draft values.
2. **Activity Log**: The system logs every draft save. In `draft.handler.ts`:
   ```typescript
   logDraftActivity(context, id, slug, displayTitle, 'draft saved')
   ```
   This writes a record to the `activity_logs` table containing the `user_name` and `user_email` of the actor.
3. **DataTable & Shadcn UI**: The dashboard already provides a reusable `@/components/ui/data-table` component that can render a list of entries with custom columns. All dashboard UI elements MUST reuse existing Shadcn UI components located in `@/components/ui/` (such as `Button`, `Dialog`, `DropdownMenu`, etc.) to maintain visual and functional consistency.
4. **API and Client**: Hono handles backend routing under `/api` in `apps/api/src/factory.ts`. Axios and React Query (`useQuery` / `useMutation`) manage client-side fetching in the dashboard.

